course: dictionary
lesson: 13782
title: Medical words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hospital words can sound strange, but the words around them often give clues. Read the whole sentence and ask what would make sense. «The nurse put an intravenous drip into Sam's arm.» A nurse, an arm and a drip tell you this is about medicine being given to a patient.
explain: Intravenous means going into a vein, the tube that carries blood back to the heart. «The medicine went straight into his blood through an intravenous needle.» The word straight and the word blood are your clues: the medicine goes directly into the body, not into the stomach.
explain: Doctors often shorten long words. IV is the short form of intravenous, so «Mia's IV was checked every hour» means her intravenous drip was checked. When you see IV in a hospital story, swap in intravenous and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Intravenous means going into a vein.
fact: A vein is a tube that carries blood back to the heart.
fact: An intravenous drip gives medicine, food or fluid straight into the blood.
fact: IV is the short form of intravenous, and «an IV» often means an intravenous drip.
fact: «She needed intravenous fluids because she could not drink.» Here intravenous means the fluid went into her vein.
exercise: «The nurse set up an intravenous drip for Sam.» What does intravenous mean? | *Going into a vein | Going into the stomach | Going into the ears | Going out through the skin
exercise: «Mia's IV was checked every hour.» What does IV stand for? | Injection | Intensive | Internal | *Intravenous
exercise: «The medicine went straight into his blood through an intravenous needle.» Where did the medicine go? | Onto the skin as a cream | Into the lungs to be breathed in | *Straight into the blood, through a vein | Into the stomach to be digested
test: «She needed intravenous fluids because she could not drink.» What do intravenous fluids do? | Make the room warm | Help her hear better | *Give fluid straight into the blood through a vein | Clean the teeth
test: «A vein carries blood back to the heart.» Intravenous means going into which tube? | A muscle | A bone | *A vein | An artery
exam: What is an intravenous drip? | A plaster covering a cut | A sweet drink to fill you up | *Medicine or fluid given straight into a vein | A pill swallowed with water
